
LMS-PROJECT Backend - API Documentation

Overview
This document describes the REST API endpoints for the lms-backend. All endpoints are JSON-based. Authentication uses JWT in the Authorization header as: Bearer <token>.

Base URL
- Local: http://localhost:PORT/api (replace PORT with your server port)

User Endpoints

1) Create User
- POST /users/create
- Description: Register a new user.
- Body (application/json):
  {
    "name": "string",
    "email": "user@example.com",
    "password": "string"
  }
- Success (201):
  {
    "success": true,
    "message": "User created successfully",
    "user": { "id": number, "name": "string", "email": "string" }
  }
- Errors: 400 for validation or if user already exists.

2) Login User
- GET /users/login
- Description: Authenticate user and receive a JWT token.
- Query params or body (JSON):
  {
    "email": "user@example.com",
    "password": "string"
  }
- Success (200):
  {
    "success": true,
    "message": "Login successful",
    "token": "<jwt>"
  }
- Errors: 401 for invalid credentials.

3) Get Users (Admin / List)
- GET /users
- Description: Fetch paginated list of users with optional search, filtering and sorting. Requires authentication.
- Query params:
  - page (number, default 1)
  - limit (number, default 10)
  - search (string) — searches name and email (case-insensitive)
  - sortby (string) — supported fields include id
  - sortorder (string) — asc or desc
  - role (string) — filter by role
- Headers:
  - Authorization: Bearer <token>
- Success (200):
  {
    "success": true,
    "pagination": {
      "totalUsers": number,
      "currentPage": number,
      "totalPages": number,
      "limit": number
    },
    "filters": { "search": "", "sortby": "id", "sortorder": "desc", "role": "" },
    "users": [ { "id": number, "name": "string", "email": "string", "role": "string" }, ... ]
  }

4) Get Profile
- GET /users/profile
- Description: Get authenticated user's profile. Requires Authorization header.
- Headers:
  - Authorization: Bearer <token>
- Success (200):
  {
    "success": true,
    "user": { "id": number, "name": "string", "email": "string" }
  }
- Errors: 401 if token missing/invalid; 404 if user not found.

Course Endpoints

5) Create Course
- POST /courses/create
- Description: Create a new course.
- Body (application/json):
  {
    "title": "string",
    "description": "string",
    "price": number
  }
- Success (201):
  {
    "success": true,
    "menubar": "Course created successfully",
    "course": {
      "id": number,
      "title": "string",
      "description": "string",
      "price": number,
      "createdAt": "string"
    }
  }
- Errors: 400 when any field is missing.

6) Get Courses
- GET /courses
- Description: Fetch paginated list of courses with optional search, filtering and sorting.
- Query params:
  - page (number, default 1)
  - limit (number, default 10)
  - search (string) — searches course title (case-insensitive)
  - sortby (string, default createdAt)
  - order (string, default desc)
  - minimumPrice (number, default 0)
  - maxPrice (number, default 100000)
- Success (200):
  {
    "success": true,
    "pagination": {
      "totalCourses": number,
      "currentPage": number,
      "totalPages": number,
      "limit": number
    },
    "filters": {
      "search": "",
      "minimumPrice": number,
      "maxPrice": number,
      "sortby": "createdAt",
      "order": "desc"
    },
    "courses": [ { "id": number, "title": "string", "description": "string", "price": number, "createdAt": "string" }, ... ]
  }

Error Handling
- API returns HTTP status codes and JSON error messages. Common responses: 400 (bad request), 401 (unauthorized), 404 (not found), 500 (server error).

Notes
- Passwords are stored hashed using bcrypt.
- JWT secret must be set in environment: JWT_SECRET
- Route paths in this project are mounted under /api in index.js.

Contact
- Repository: check project root for README and route configuration for exact paths.
